    "prompt": "[Verse 1]\nYou leave your coat beside the kitchen chair\nRain in the hallway, water everywhere\nI read the note you folded into four\nOne careful sentence saying nothing more\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nIf you are tired of carrying the blame\nPut down the weight, forget my name\n\n[Chorus]\nYou don't have to disappear tonight\nYou can leave the porch light on inside\nI won't ask you to explain the scars\nJust tell me where you are\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe kettle clicks, the room begins to cool\nYour photograph is face-down by the stool\nI count the tiles and wait for morning's sound\nA small red button rolling on the ground\n\n[Bridge]\nTake what you need, take the old blue shirt\nTake every promise that was made to hurt\nBut if you turn around before you go\nYou'll find me by the door\n\n[Chorus]\nYou don't have to disappear tonight\nYou can leave the porch light on inside\nI won't ask you to explain the scars\nJust tell me where you are\n\n[Outro]\nJust tell me where you are\nJust tell me where you are",
